# Draft delivery lineage exported by the Proposal Workbench (BRSF software-development profile). Refine, then validate with the BRSF validator.

ex:Mission a backlog:Mission ; rdfs:label "Blockchain-Based Document Verification System"@en ; backlog:hasMissionStatement "The project aims to provide document issuers and document verifiers with a simple web application for checking the integrity of PDF documents. The system allows document issuers to register document fingerprints on a blockchain and enables document verifiers to detect modified documents without storing the original document contents on the blockchain." ; backlog:hasMissionOutcome "Document verifiers will be able to determine whether a received PDF matches a fingerprint previously registered by the designated document issuer. The system will provide a clear verification result without exposing the contents of the original document." ; backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_SessionDrafted .
ex:Lineage a backlog:Lineage ; backlog:lineageForMission ex:Mission ; backlog:adoptsObligationSet backlog:OS_SDLC_v2 .
ex:Customer1 a backlog:Stakeholder ; rdfs:label "Koel Electronics"@en ; rdfs:comment "Customer (operator): A simple web application for registering and verifying digital documents using blockchain technology."@en .
ex:EndUser1 a backlog:Stakeholder ; rdfs:label "Document issuer"@en ; rdfs:comment "End user: Staff members of the customer organization who are responsible for preparing, issuing and distributing official PDF documents, certificates and reports to their recipients. - They select PDF documents, generate SHA-256 fingerprints, register these fingerprints on the blockchain using an authorized wallet and download registration receipts after successful transactions. (occasional, Browser)"@en .
ex:EndUser2 a backlog:Stakeholder ; rdfs:label "Document verifier"@en ; rdfs:comment "End user: Individuals who receive digital PDF documents from the customer organization and need to check whether the received documents match the original versions registered by the document issuer. - They select received PDF documents, calculate their SHA-256 fingerprints, compare the fingerprints with blockchain registration records and view the verification results to check document integrity. (occasional, Browser)"@en .
ex:Scope a backlog:ScopeStatement ; backlog:scopeForMission ex:Mission ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage ; backlog:coversArea ex:A1, ex:A2 ; backlog:requiresDeliverable ex:D1, ex:D2, ex:D3, ex:D4 ; backlog:hasScopeExclusion ex:X1, ex:X2, ex:X3 .
ex:A1 a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "Document Processing"@en ; backlog:areaLocation "Web browser" ; backlog:areaMeasure "One PDF at a time" .
ex:A2 a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "Registration and Verification"@en ; backlog:areaLocation "Web browser" ; backlog:areaMeasure "One issuer and one smart contract are planned" .
ex:D1 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "PDF selection and SHA-256 hashing"@en ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:A1 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:D2 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "JSON-LD registration receipt"@en ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:A1 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:D3 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Issuer-only document registration"@en ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:A2 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:D4 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Document verification and result display"@en ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:A2 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:X1 a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Mainnet deployment and real payments"@en ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "To avoid real transaction costs and financial risks." .
ex:X2 a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Original document storage on blockchain"@en ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "To protect document contents and reduce storage costs." .
ex:X3 a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Multiple issuers and identity certification"@en ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "To keep the project manageable for a single developer." .
ex:G1 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "Enable reliable document verification"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Mission ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A2 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "To allow document verifiers to detect changes in registered PDF documents." .
ex:G2 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "Complete document processing and receipt generation"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Scope ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A1 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "To ensure that PDF hashing and registration receipt generation are completed." .
ex:G3 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "Keep implementation within the agreed project scope"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Containment ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A2 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "To avoid unauthorized registration, original document publication and out-of-scope features." .
ex:Spec a backlog:Specification ; backlog:hasSpecificationText "The system shall allow users to select PDF documents through a simple web interface. Each document shall be limited to a maximum file size of 10 MB. The application shall calculate a SHA-256 hash locally in the browser. The designated document issuer shall be able to register the hash using a Solidity smart contract on the Ethereum Sepolia test network. Document verifiers shall be able to check whether a calculated hash exists in the contract. The system shall display registered, not registered or an appropriate error message. Duplicate and unauthorized registrations shall be rejected. A JSON-LD receipt shall be available after successful registration. Original PDF contents shall not be stored on the blockchain." .
ex:Scen1 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Nominal ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given a registered PDF, when the verifier selects the original file, then the system displays Registered." .
ex:Scen2 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Rejection ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given an unauthorized wallet, when it attempts to register a document, then the smart contract rejects the transaction." .
ex:Scen3 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Boundary ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given a valid PDF with a size of exactly 10 MB, when the user selects it, then the application accepts the file." .
ex:Scen4 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Absent ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given that no PDF has been selected, when the user attempts verification, then the application displays an error message." .
ex:O1 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Achieve correct document verification results"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G1 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "Count correct verification results for two original and two modified PDF documents." ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0 of 4 verified" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "4 of 4 verified" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase .
ex:O2 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Complete document processing functions"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G2 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "Count successful SHA-256 hashing and JSON-LD receipt generation tests." ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0 of 2" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "2 of 2" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase .
ex:O3 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Maintain the agreed implementation boundaries"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G3 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "Count unauthorized registrations, raw PDF publications and implemented excluded features during testing and code review." ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "0" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Hold .
ex:Model_Activity a backlog:ModelArtifact ; backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_ActivityDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ; backlog:declaresState "The process starts when the user selects a PDF document. The application checks the file type and size. If the file is invalid, an error message is displayed. Otherwise, the SHA-256 fingerprint is calculated. The user selects registration or verification. Registration requires the authorized issuer wallet and transaction confirmation. If the transaction succeeds, a receipt can be downloaded. If it fails, an error is displayed. Verification reads the blockchain record and displays the verification result. The process ends after the result is shown." .
ex:Model_Sequence a backlog:ModelArtifact ; backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_SequenceDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ; backlog:declaresState "The document issuer selects a PDF through the browser interface. The browser sends the document bytes to the Web Crypto API locally and receives a SHA-256 fingerprint. The browser requests transaction approval from MetaMask. MetaMask submits the fingerprint to the smart contract. The contract checks authorization and returns a transaction result. After confirmation, the browser generates a receipt. The document verifier selects a received PDF. The browser calculates its fingerprint and sends a read-only request to the smart contract. The contract returns the registration status, and the browser displays the result to the verifier." .
ex:Model_Class a backlog:ModelArtifact ; backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_ClassDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ; backlog:declaresState "The system contains three main classes: DocumentFingerprint, Registration and Receipt. DocumentFingerprint contains the SHA-256 digest and file size. Registration contains the document digest, authorized issuer address and registration timestamp. Receipt contains the digest, issuer address, transaction hash and contract address. One document fingerprint can have zero or one blockchain registration. A confirmed registration can generate a receipt. Original PDF contents remain in the browser and are not permanently stored by the application." .
ex:Backlog a backlog:Backlog ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage ; backlog:appliesDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD .
ex:DoD a backlog:DefinitionOfDone ; backlog:hasDoDCriterion ex:DoD1, ex:DoD2, ex:DoD3 .
ex:DoD1 a backlog:DoDCriterion ; rdfs:label "SHA-256 document fingerprints are generated correctly."@en ; backlog:hasCheckQuery "Compare the generated fingerprint with a reference SHA-256 hash of the same PDF." .
ex:DoD2 a backlog:DoDCriterion ; rdfs:label "Original and modified documents are correctly identified."@en ; backlog:hasCheckQuery "Verify two original and two modified PDF documents and check the displayed results." .
ex:DoD3 a backlog:DoDCriterion ; rdfs:label "Unauthorized and duplicate registrations are rejected."@en ; backlog:hasCheckQuery "Attempt registration using an unauthorized wallet and an already registered fingerprint." .
ex:Initiative a backlog:Initiative ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:hasInitiativeKind backlog:Kind_InitialDevelopment ; backlog:decomposesInto ex:E1, ex:E2, ex:E3 .
ex:E1 a backlog:Epic ; rdfs:label "PDF Processing and Receipt"@en ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:pursuesObjective ex:O2 ; backlog:decomposesInto ex:S1, ex:S2 .
ex:E2 a backlog:Epic ; rdfs:label "Document Verification"@en ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:pursuesObjective ex:O1 ; backlog:decomposesInto ex:S3, ex:S4 .
ex:E3 a backlog:Epic ; rdfs:label "Blockchain Registration"@en ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:pursuesObjective ex:O3 ; backlog:decomposesInto ex:S5, ex:S6 .
ex:S1 a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "to generate a SHA-256 fingerprint from a PDF document"@en ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:asRole "Document issuer" ; backlog:wantsCapability "to generate a SHA-256 fingerprint from a PDF document" ; backlog:soThat "I can identify the exact version of the document" ; backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasApplicableConcern backlog:Concern_Data ; backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion ex:AC1 ; backlog:hasPriorityScore ex:Score1 .
ex:AC1 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; backlog:hasGherkinText "Given a valid PDF document, when the document issuer selects the file, then the application calculates and displays its SHA-256 fingerprint." .
ex:Score1 a backlog:PriorityScore ; backlog:scoredByMethod backlog:Method_WSJF ; backlog:hasScoreValue "13"^^xsd:decimal .
ex:S2 a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "to download a registration receipt"@en ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:asRole "Document issuer" ; backlog:wantsCapability "to download a registration receipt" ; backlog:soThat "I can retain evidence of document registration" ; backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasApplicableConcern backlog:Concern_Data ; backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion ex:AC2 ; backlog:hasPriorityScore ex:Score2 .
ex:AC2 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; backlog:hasGherkinText "Given a successfully confirmed registration transaction, when the document issuer clicks the download button, then the application downloads a JSON-LD receipt containing the fingerprint and transaction information." .
ex:Score2 a backlog:PriorityScore ; backlog:scoredByMethod backlog:Method_WSJF ; backlog:hasScoreValue "4.3"^^xsd:decimal .
ex:S3 a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "to verify an original PDF document"@en ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:asRole "Document verifier" ; backlog:wantsCapability "to verify an original PDF document" ; backlog:soThat "I can check whether it matches a registered document" ; backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasApplicableConcern backlog:Concern_Interaction ; backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion ex:AC3 ; backlog:hasPriorityScore ex:Score3 .
ex:AC3 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; backlog:hasGherkinText "Given a previously registered PDF document, when the document verifier selects the identical file and clicks Verify, then the system displays Registered." .
ex:Score3 a backlog:PriorityScore ; backlog:scoredByMethod backlog:Method_WSJF ; backlog:hasScoreValue "8.7"^^xsd:decimal .
ex:S4 a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "to check whether a document has been modified"@en ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:asRole "Document verifier" ; backlog:wantsCapability "to check whether a document has been modified" ; backlog:soThat "I can identify files that do not match a registered fingerprint" ; backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasApplicableConcern backlog:Concern_Interaction ; backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion ex:AC4 ; backlog:hasPriorityScore ex:Score4 .
ex:AC4 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; backlog:hasGherkinText "Given a modified version of a registered PDF whose new fingerprint has not been registered, when the document verifier checks the file, then the system displays Not Registered." .
ex:Score4 a backlog:PriorityScore ; backlog:scoredByMethod backlog:Method_WSJF ; backlog:hasScoreValue "12"^^xsd:decimal .
ex:S5 a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "to restrict document registration to my authorized wallet"@en ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:asRole "Document issuer" ; backlog:wantsCapability "to restrict document registration to my authorized wallet" ; backlog:soThat "unauthorized users cannot register documents in my name" ; backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasApplicableConcern backlog:Concern_Security ; backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion ex:AC5 ; backlog:hasPriorityScore ex:Score5 .
ex:AC5 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; backlog:hasGherkinText "Given a wallet address that is not authorized to register documents, when the wallet attempts to submit a new fingerprint, then the smart contract rejects the transaction and leaves its stored records unchanged." .
ex:Score5 a backlog:PriorityScore ; backlog:scoredByMethod backlog:Method_WSJF ; backlog:hasScoreValue "8.7"^^xsd:decimal .
ex:S6 a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "to register a document fingerprint on the blockchain"@en ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:asRole "Document issuer" ; backlog:wantsCapability "to register a document fingerprint on the blockchain" ; backlog:soThat "document verifiers can check it later" ; backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasApplicableConcern backlog:Concern_Security ; backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion ex:AC6 ; backlog:hasPriorityScore ex:Score6 .
ex:AC6 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; backlog:hasGherkinText "Given an authorized issuer wallet and an unregistered document fingerprint, when the issuer confirms the registration transaction, then the smart contract stores the fingerprint and its registration timestamp. A repeated registration of the same fingerprint shall be rejected." .
ex:Score6 a backlog:PriorityScore ; backlog:scoredByMethod backlog:Method_WSJF ; backlog:hasScoreValue "9.7"^^xsd:decimal .
